---
description: Enforces strict dependency rules for the Domain layer.
globs:
  - "**/domain/**/*.dart"
type: AutoAttached
---
CRITICAL: Domain layer code MUST NOT import or depend on:
- Any Flutter UI packages (`package:flutter/**`).
- Any Data layer implementations (`package:*/data/**`).
- Any Presentation layer components (`package:*/ui/**`).
- Specific database, network, or device APIs.
- Third-party service implementations (Firebase, AWS, etc.).

Allowed dependencies:
- Dart SDK (`dart:*`).
- Core packages like `freezed_annotation`, `equatable`.
- Other Domain layer components (entities, other use cases, repository interfaces).
- Approved, framework-agnostic utility packages.
- Functional programming utilities (e.g., `dartz` for Either type).
- Dependency injection annotations (e.g., `injectable`).

Best practices:
- Define abstract repository interfaces for data access.
- Use Either<Failure, Success> pattern for error handling.
- Keep entities immutable with proper value equality.
